  speakerName: Ronnie
  speakerPortrait: {fileID: 0}
  dialogueText: 'Now it''s your turn to introduce yourself.

    In Ilokano, ''ti
    nagan ko ket...'' means ''my name is...''

    The words ''ti nagan ko ket''
    form the fixed part of the phrase. You then add your own name.

    For example:
    ''Ti nagan ko ket Jom.''

    Now, try saying ''ti nagan ko ket ___'' yourself.'
